{"comment_text": {"ja29:0.1": "", "ja29:0.2": "", "ja29:0.3": "", "ja29:0.4": "", "ja29:1.1": "An ox raised by an old woman earns money for his “mother” by pulling a heavy load across a deep river. ", "ja29:1.2": "", "ja29:1.3": "", "ja29:1.4": "", "ja29:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja29:0.1": "<article id='ja29'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja29:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja29:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja29:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja29:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja29:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja29:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja29:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja29:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja29:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja29:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja29:0.3": "Kuruṅgavagga ", "ja29:0.4": "9. Kaṇhajātaka ", "ja29:1.1": "“Yato yato garu dhuraṁ, ", "ja29:1.2": "yato gambhīravattanī; ", "ja29:1.3": "Tadāssu kaṇhaṁ yuñjanti, ", "ja29:1.4": "svāssu taṁ vahate dhuran”ti. ", "ja29:2.1": "Kaṇhajātakaṁ navamaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja29:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 29 ", "ja29:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja29:0.3": "The Four-horned Antelope ", "ja29:0.4": "The Ox Named Black: a past life story ", "ja29:1.1": "No matter how heavy the load, ", "ja29:1.2": "or how deep the passage, ", "ja29:1.3": "when they harness Black, ", "ja29:1.4": "he pulls that load. ", "ja29:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja29:0.1": "", "ja29:0.2": "", "ja29:0.3": "", "ja29:0.4": "", "ja29:1.1": "ms22J_62, msdiv29, pts-vp-pli1.196", "ja29:1.2": "", "ja29:1.3": "", "ja29:1.4": "", "ja29:2.1": "ms22J_63"}, "keys_order": ["ja29:0.1", "ja29:0.2", "ja29:0.3", "ja29:0.4", "ja29:1.1", "ja29:1.2", "ja29:1.3", "ja29:1.4", "ja29:2.1"]}